    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ex32dqr",
      "content": "Animal husbandry is the management, breeding, and care of farm animals including cattle, buffalo, goat, sheep, poultry, pig, fish, and honeybees. It accounts for about 4% of India's GDP and 26% of agricultural GDP. India has the world's largest cattle and buffalo population."
    },
